# The server-rendered pages come first: they are real paths on the public domain, and
# the SPA catch-all below would otherwise swallow them and answer with index.html.
#
# They are rendered by the API (server/src/seo/), which in production is a different
# origin — so they have to be proxied here, or they end up as a second website on the
# API's hostname competing with this one. Uncomment and set the host. See PRODUCTION.md,
# "City landing pages, robots.txt and sitemap.xml".
#
# /nadlan/*     https://API-HOST/nadlan/:splat   200
# /sitemap.xml  https://API-HOST/sitemap.xml     200
# /robots.txt   https://API-HOST/robots.txt      200

# SPA: every other path (e.g. /agency/6816047?listing=…) is served by index.html and
# resolved client-side by react-router.
/*    /index.html   200
